            "result_text": "Done! I've created `/app/run.py` with the `run_tasks` async function that:\n\n**Features:**\n- Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to limit concurrent execution to `max_concurrent`\n- Accepts tasks as a list of async callables and runs them with the concurrency limit\n- Handles `KeyboardInterrupt` gracefully: when interrupted, it cancels pending tasks but waits for them to finish, ensuring their cleanup code (finally blocks, async context managers) runs properly\n- Can be imported as `from run import run_tasks`\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Creates a semaphore limiting concurrent tasks\n2. Wraps each task to acquire the semaphore before running\n3. Creates explicit Task objects so they can be cancelled if needed\n4. On `KeyboardInterrupt`: cancels all tasks, then waits for them with `return_exceptions=True` so cleanup runs, then re-raises the interrupt\n\nThe implementation was tested and verified to properly limit concurrency and execute cleanup code even when interrupted."
